# Wireframe: Toast Notification

## Purpose & Flow Context

Provides feedback on shortcut actions. Entry: shortcut action completes. Exit: auto-dismiss or user dismisses.

---

## Notation Legend

| Symbol | Meaning | Symbol | Meaning |
|--------|---------|--------|---------|
| `[...]` | Button / interactive element | `[>...▼]` | Dropdown |
| `_______` | Text input / editable field | `[X]` | Close / dismiss |
| `⚠` | Warning / due date | `📎N` | N attachments |
| `💬N` | N comments | `🔗` | Card relationship |
| `👤` | User / mention | `○ ●` | Radio unselected / selected |

## Accessibility — Shared Conventions

All interactive screens inherit these. Per-screen specifics noted where they diverge.

| Concern | Convention |
|---------|------------|
| Landmarks | `header`, `main`, `aside`, `contentinfo` |
| Heading order | One `h1` per screen, `h2` for sections |
| Accessible names | Icon-only controls get `aria-label` |
| Keyboard | Tab, Enter/Space, Escape, Arrow keys |
| Target size | ≥24×24 CSS px reservation |
| Non-color intent | Icon + text, never color alone |

---

## Layout Regions

**Grid**: 12-column layout. Spacing cadence: 8px rhythm intent.

**App-shell**: Shared header + nav + container. Regions:

| Region | Content | Notes |
|--------|---------|-------|
| Toast Container | Fixed position (bottom-right) | Stack of toasts |
| Toast | Icon + Message (+ [Close] on error) | Auto-dismiss or manual |

**Content hierarchy** (by visual priority):
1. Icon (status indicator)
2. Message text
3. Close button (for error toasts)

```
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|                                                +--------------+  |
|                                                | ✓  Message  |  |
|                                                |    [X]      |  |
|                                                +--------------+  |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
```

*Legend: [{Button}] [Input] [Link] [#Heading] [>Dropdown] [Avatar] [Icon]*

## Components & Affordances

| Element | DS Component | Behavior | Edge Cases |
|---------|-------------|----------|------------|
| Toast Container | div | Fixed position, stacks toasts | — |
| Icon | svg | Status indicator | — |
| Message | span | Action feedback text | — |
| [Close] | Button | Dismisses toast | **Error toasts only** — success/info auto-dismiss; not rendered for non-error variants |

## Data Display

No data display — feedback only.

## Content & Microcopy Intent

| Slot | Intent | Notes |
|------|--------|-------|
| Success Message | "Shortcut updated" | Positive feedback |
| Error Message | "This key combination is already in use" | Error feedback |
| Info Message | "Shortcut disabled" | Neutral feedback |
| [Close] | "Dismiss notification" | Error toasts only; success/info rely on auto-dismiss |

## States

### Populated (Default)

Toast visible with message and auto-dismiss timer.

```
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|  ✓ Shortcut updated                                             |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
```

### Empty

No toasts displayed.

### Loading

Not applicable — toasts don't load.

### Error

```
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|  ⚠ This key combination is already in use         [X]           |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
```

### Success / Confirmation

```
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|  ✓ Shortcut updated                                             |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
```

## Responsive

| Breakpoint | Changes |
|------------|---------|
| Desktop (>1024px) | Fixed bottom-right position |
| Tablet (768-1024px) | Same position |
| Mobile (<768px) | Full-width at bottom |

## Accessibility — Screen Composition

| Concern | Implementation |
|---------|----------------|
| Landmarks | (not part of main landmarks) |
| Heading order | N/A |
| Reading / Focus order | Icon → Message → Close |
| Accessible names | Close button: aria-label="Dismiss notification" |
| Keyboard operability | Esc to dismiss |
| Target size | ≥24×24 CSS px on Close button |
| Focus not obscured | Toast doesn't obscure focus |
| Non-color intent | Icon + text + color |

---

## Assumptions & Open Questions

| # | Assumption / Gap | Rationale | Action Required |
|---|-----------------|-----------|-----------------|
| 1 | **Create Issue Modal** — referenced by user-flows as destination of "C" shortcut; not wireframed here | Owned by the Issue Creation module, not the Keyboard module. The keyboard module triggers it; the Issue module defines its UI. | Issue Creation module must provide its own wireframes. |
| 2 | **Status Change Modal** — referenced by user-flows as destination of "S" shortcut; not wireframed here | Owned by the Issue Actions module. The keyboard module triggers the status cycle; the Issue module defines the modal. | Issue Actions module must provide its own wireframes. |
| 3 | **Assign Modal** — referenced by user-flows as destination of "A" shortcut; not wireframed here | Owned by the Issue Actions module (assignee picker). | Issue Actions module must provide its own wireframes. |
| 4 | **Label Modal** — referenced by user-flows as destination of "L" shortcut; not wireframed here | Owned by the Issue Actions module (label picker). | Issue Actions module must provide its own wireframes. |
| 5 | **Component-contract a11y** (pixel contrast, focus-appearance) deferred to design-system | Per the authoring-wireframes bar: the wireframe owns screen-composition a11y; the DS owns per-component contrast/focus. No DS hi-fi pass exists yet. | Design-system must define per-component contrast + focus-appearance contracts before hi-fi pass. |
